From 3206446dc233b9233315134a1880849328b3fe5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:13:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audit: release-tag bypass check for mint-released repos (#25)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements trellis#34's contract as a conformance audit: a repo that
releases via mint (a workflow on `push: tags: [v*]`, a `.release/` dir, or a
call to mint's release-cut.yml) must give its release identity a
tag-creation path — an `always` bypass_actor on every ACTIVE ruleset whose
`creation` rule covers refs/tags/v*. Without one, `git push origin v1.2.3`
fails with GH013 and the GitHub Release/binaries/provenance silently never
land; this surfaces it as a repo-config finding at the gate instead.

- scripts/audit/release-tags.ts — Deno runner modeled on actions.ts:
  `gh repo list` → trees/contents → rulesets?targets=tag&includes_parents
  → per-ruleset detail; prints a per-repo markdown table (repo,
  mint-released, restricted, bypass, verdict, evidence) + summary.
  Report-only (exit 0); --strict exits 1 on FAIL, --fail-unknown also on
  UNKNOWN; --release-actor selects the identity (any | github-actions |
  org-admin | integration:<id> | team:<id> | role:<id> | deploy-key:<id>),
  defaulting to any `always` actor while trellis#34 leaves the declaration
  site open. bypass_actors absent from the API response (token lacks write
  access to the ruleset) scores UNKNOWN, never a false PASS.
- scripts/audit/release-tags-lib.ts — the pure logic (ref_name fnmatch,
  restriction test, mint detection, scoring, table rendering).
- scripts/audit/release-tags_test.ts + fixtures/ — 13 unit tests against
  fixture JSON in the GitHub ruleset API shape (node:assert, no new deps).
- .github/workflows/release-tags-audit.yml — two jobs split by credential:
  `pr` (pull_request, github.token only → restricted repos read UNKNOWN)
  and `org` (schedule + workflow_dispatch, default branch, mints the
  org-admin App token as open-prs.yml does). PR-modified code never runs
  with the admin credential.
- deno.json tasks audit:release-tags[:strict], test:audit; README section +
  row; cspell: fnmatch, ignore fixtures.

Token scope: rulesets LIST is readable with contents:read, but
bypass_actors needs write access to the ruleset (admin:org for org
rulesets; enterprise owner for the enterprise-level refs/tags/* one).

Closes #25

